 r←Test_RefreshStaleLock url;Assert;dead;res;state
⍝ Check a refresh serialisation lock orphaned by a dead worker thread does not
⍝ wedge refresh permanently. Forges the lock state directly: the test suite shares
⍝ the interpreter with the application, so #.DCMS.GLOBAL is reachable.
 r←0
 Assert←##.Assert
 state←#.DCMS.GLOBAL.refresh
 :Trap 0
     'Refresh already running at start of test'Assert ##.WaitRefreshIdle 150
    ⍝ Forge a lock held by a thread number far above any the interpreter would
    ⍝ allocate (new threads take the lowest free number), so it cannot be live.
     dead←1000+⌈/0,⎕TNUMS
     state.(running thread pending)←1 dead 0
     res←('POST'Authed url,'/admin/refresh').Run
     'Expected 202 Accepted'Assert 202=res.HttpStatus
     'Orphaned lock wedged refresh: trigger was queued behind a dead thread'Assert~∨/'pending'⍷res.Data.message
     'Lock not transferred off the dead thread'Assert state.thread≠dead
     'Refresh did not complete'Assert ##.WaitRefreshIdle 300
     r←1
 :EndTrap
⍝ Teardown: never leave a forged or orphaned lock behind for later tests
 {}##.WaitRefreshIdle 300
 :If state.running∧~state.thread∊⎕TNUMS
     state.(running thread pending)←0 ¯1 0
 :EndIf
